table  politician  um  and uh  you know  only only a democrat that had as much  negative baggage as hubert humphrey  could have possibly lost to  thank you  um being a former maoist  what you've been saying uh leads me to  remember mao ze tung saying that history  is like a boiling pot for decades it may  everything may be beneath the surface  and nothing appears but then all of a  sudden in one year or in a few years  decades occur and that's what happened  in 1968 basically four or five ten years  occurred in that one year and in that  decade you could say decades occurred in  the 60s in terms of things being uh yeah  and and you know  i think there may be a lot of things  going on now that people don't see  there were millions who demonstrated  against the war in iraq there are a lot  of things going on a lot of it  isn't that easy to see because it's not  on the street it's in the internet  tom hayden said to me that in  the early 1960s when he was a student at  university of michigan and he was the  editor of the michigan daily he went out  to california and he wrote these stories  about student movements and all of these  counter culture things that were going  on and he got back to ann arbor and all  of the his faculty advisors said why are  you making up this stuff none of this is  happening and it took about two years  more before you know everybody saw that  these things were happening  let me make one other comment which is  about  you're talking about a lot of good  things were done and i feel in the 50s  60s and 70s is basically the greatest  democratic movement in american history  you figure in 1950 women had the right  to vote but essentially no other rights  african-americans had no rights latinos  asian-americans lesbians and gays  handicaps we're talking 60 to 80 percent  of the population of america gained huge  rights in those decades and we should be  very proud what we accomplished in those  years yeah but we need to accomplish  more the far r