e johnson years  the assassination of martin luther king  who held a certain  element of  idealism  and  even things  even things in my own case i i was in  the foreign service  and working for the u.s agency for  international development in nigeria  during this period  and one of them during the biafra yes  exactly and one of the senses that i had  over there and i had it when i came back  to the states off and on during that  same year  was that the idealism of of africa the  hopes for nigeria  uh the great writers of sryanka  and these people were kind of dashed by  by the tribalism and again  essentially the war so yeah i mean the  emotional uh psychological impact of the  biafran war  because as you say i mean nigeria was  one of the new emerging nations that had  uh that that people had the greatest  hopes for  um  and you know this too was was on tv and  in the media and we all saw these  starving children every day and it  it had a a huge  psychological effect on people all over  the world so in a sense just generally  in 68 my my sense of it was that much of  the idealism of earlier in the decade  had run into great difficulty in seeing  it played out and and progress being  made and there was a certain degree of  of reaction to it that of the  hopelessness of the situation which led  as a matter of fact i made a note uh  when you were talking about the poets  well here's here's one thing you have in  in popular culture  the the musical hair with the first  nudity that i ever saw on the stage  unbelievably 1968 right  before that  the culture that i was more feeling you  know raising in the sun to kill a  mockingbird more serious and and less of  a kind of frustrated lashing out at  things that weren't well i mean there  was a lot of really serious theater at  68. hair was you know  what was hair about it was about the age  of aquarius i think yeah  it was part of this whole  thing of let's try to find out what the  hippies are doing  thank you thank you  